# The Anti-Fibonacci Paradox: An Interactive Investigation

The famous Fibonacci rule adds two neighboring terms. This proposed reversal seems to avoid that sum, yet its use of the *least positive integer* creates a surprise: only one number is forbidden, so $1$ is almost always available.

